package alliance_member

// AllianceMemberMirror is what a game server reads of a player's alliance
// guard: which alliance they are in, and whether a join is still open. The
// guard's id is the player's, so "which guild am I in" is one mirror read
// with no lookup service (plan §2.5), followed by the alliance's own mirror.
//
// The roster is the authority on membership; the guard follows it (the same
// transaction on one instance, an effect across two). A mirror of the guard
// may therefore lag the roster by that effect plus the mirror's own
// staleness — fine for showing, never for deciding: every write is decided by
// the alliance service.
//
//roost:mirror entityKind=EntityKindAllianceMember coll=alliance_member
type AllianceMemberMirror struct {
	AllianceID        int64 `bson:"alliance_id"`
	PendingAllianceID int64 `bson:"pending_alliance_id"`
	RewardPeriod      int64 `bson:"reward_period"`
}
